WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.520
Maruo Eiichiro 
Ide Yoshiaki

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:04.500
<i>I won!</i>

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:07.020
You did it, Ei-chan!

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:10.410
Ei-chan, you pulled it off!

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:11.530
Congratulations!

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:14.790
<i>I won.</i>

00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:18.570
You both did great!

00:00:18.570 --> 00:00:20.040
I really got excited!

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:23.660
Yosshi! You really are the best!

00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:25.920
Even when you lose, you look awesome!

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:27.920
Yeah, you looked awesome!

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:29.800
Great job, Yosshi!

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:30.920
You did so well!

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:36.320
Damn...

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:37.470
But, hey...

00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:40.930
That was the best match ever, 
so I guess it's all good.

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:46.840
Here, give 'em a little show.

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:49.190
Wha... Oh, right.

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:50.970
You're both awesome!

00:00:50.970 --> 00:00:52.190
That was inspiring!

00:00:52.730 --> 00:00:56.320
Maruo! You'd better work twice 
as hard for Ide at the All-Japan!

00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:00.660
<i>I really beat Ide-kun...</i>

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:02.920
<i>How many more times</i>

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:05.160
<i>will I get to hear a roaring crowd like this?</i>

00:01:08.330 --> 00:01:10.670
<i>Now I can move forward.</i>

00:02:45.490 --> 00:02:49.480
A Rude First Meeting

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:53.230
Ei-chan!

00:02:53.630 --> 00:02:56.730
Congrats on officially making it 
to the All-Japan Junior!

00:02:57.340 --> 00:02:58.990
Congratulations, Maruo-kun!

00:02:58.990 --> 00:03:00.150
Thank you.

00:03:00.150 --> 00:03:03.110
But seriously, that was an incredible match.

00:03:03.110 --> 00:03:05.510
I was on the edge of my seat the whole time.

00:03:06.010 --> 00:03:09.000
But it seems as though you were 
able to overcome a huge hurdle.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:10.030
Yeah!

00:03:10.030 --> 00:03:13.020
Kageyama and Sasaki-san, 
thank you for supporting me.

00:03:13.730 --> 00:03:16.000
And I noticed when you came to watch, Nat-chan.

00:03:16.580 --> 00:03:18.260
You obviously won your match, right?

00:03:18.260 --> 00:03:21.260
Yep! Now we can go to the nationals together!

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:22.020
Yeah!

00:03:23.730 --> 00:03:24.590
Huh?

00:03:25.810 --> 00:03:28.000
I'm starting to shake <i>now</i>.

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:30.870
Huh?!

00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:33.020
Squeeze

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:34.660
It's okay.

00:03:34.660 --> 00:03:36.520
See? It stopped.

00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:39.090
Th-Thank you.

00:03:40.260 --> 00:03:41.530
<i>Wow...</i>

00:03:42.050 --> 00:03:43.780
<i>She grabbed his hand with no hesitation.</i>

00:03:44.010 --> 00:03:47.790
In all seriousness, those last 
few points were outstanding.

00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:51.790
Ah... Yeah. I was surprised myself.

00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:55.050
I was under immense pressure the whole time,

00:03:55.050 --> 00:03:57.420
but I identified it clearly 
instead of running from it,

00:03:57.420 --> 00:03:59.010
and I started doing better.

00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:01.800
Pressure

00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:03.670
In the end, I left some pressure in my mind,

00:04:03.670 --> 00:04:05.950
and I imagined erasing the rest of it.

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:09.060
Pressure

00:04:05.950 --> 00:04:10.230
Then, suddenly, both my body and 
my mind started moving faster.

00:04:11.930 --> 00:04:14.090
You were doing all that?

00:04:14.090 --> 00:04:15.270
Yeah.

00:04:15.530 --> 00:04:20.820
But I honestly don't know how 
I was able to stay so calm

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:25.740
or able to move so well 
in a situation like that.

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:28.230
Tell me about it in a little more detail.

00:04:28.230 --> 00:04:29.960
Um...

00:04:29.960 --> 00:04:33.960
I was able to see the opponent, 
the ball, and the court very well,

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:36.900
but it was almost like I 
couldn't see anything else.

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:40.250
Like I was concentrating so hard,
I couldn't even hear anything.

00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:43.010
Maybe that means you were in the zone.

00:04:43.010 --> 00:04:44.260
The "zone"?

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:47.210
It's said that even if people give it their all,

00:04:47.210 --> 00:04:51.620
they're using only about 30% of their ability.

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:56.270
Anxiety                    Exhaustion
Ability
Pressure                    Adversity

00:04:51.620 --> 00:04:56.270
Being in the zone is, in effect, 
ridding yourself of those limitations.

00:04:56.630 --> 00:04:59.850
In the sports world, athletes at the
highest level are said to have

00:04:59.850 --> 00:05:03.590
the ability to create that state of mind at will.

00:05:03.590 --> 00:05:04.280
Huh?

00:05:04.580 --> 00:05:10.330
<i>I thought it happened only because all 
the factors miraculously coincided.</i>

00:05:10.330 --> 00:05:12.040
<i>You can actually will it to happen?</i>

00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:15.300
From what I've seen, Ide seems 
like the type of player who

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:19.040
naturally starts to get in the zone 
when his matches get close.

00:05:19.370 --> 00:05:20.330
Right...

00:05:20.330 --> 00:05:24.130
But in the end, it appears 
you were able to deal with Ide

00:05:24.130 --> 00:05:26.130
by getting in the zone yourself.

00:05:27.910 --> 00:05:32.010
Looking back on it, I did have a feeling 
Ide-kun was going to get even stronger.

00:05:32.450 --> 00:05:36.690
That's why I don't think I could've won 
if I hadn't broken serve when I did.

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:41.400
In any case, this victory was 
a result you earned for yourself.

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:43.530
I earned it for myself...

00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:46.550
<i>If using my reason to visualize my pressure</i>

00:05:46.550 --> 00:05:49.910
<i>and then playing instinctively led to this,</i>

00:05:49.910 --> 00:05:54.040
<i>maybe I really did get in the zone at will.</i>

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:02.650
M-Maruo-kun, you were amazing!

00:06:02.650 --> 00:06:05.630
When you won in the end, I almost cried!

00:06:05.980 --> 00:06:08.790
<i>She has to be bummed 
about Ei-chan and Nat-chan,</i>

00:06:08.790 --> 00:06:11.480
<i>but she's trying to hide it with cheer.
It's breaking my heart.</i>

00:06:12.570 --> 00:06:17.040
Somehow I feel better after 
cheering so loudly today.

00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:18.820
Let's cheer them on at the All-Japan, too.

00:06:18.820 --> 00:06:20.770
<i>C-Cute...</i>

00:06:22.150 --> 00:06:23.710
Wh-What?

00:06:28.420 --> 00:06:32.800
I'm sorry. You went to the trouble of coming 
here, and I couldn't keep my promise.

00:06:33.650 --> 00:06:35.420
It's not your fault.

00:06:35.420 --> 00:06:36.160
Huh?

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:39.290
So when my leg gets better, 
I'll take that guy down myself!

00:06:39.980 --> 00:06:42.540
Huh? You play tennis?

00:06:42.540 --> 00:06:44.550
I'm gonna start now!

00:06:44.550 --> 00:06:46.330
Goodness, this boy...

00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:51.300
I see. So that's it...

00:06:51.570 --> 00:06:52.610
That's great!

00:06:52.610 --> 00:06:56.810
It's an awesome idea! Tennis is super fun!

00:06:57.070 --> 00:07:01.530
But defeating him means 
you'll become my rival.

00:07:01.530 --> 00:07:03.460
When that day comes, you'd better be ready!

00:07:03.460 --> 00:07:04.260
Okay!

00:07:05.540 --> 00:07:07.940
See you later, Onii-chan!

00:07:07.940 --> 00:07:09.190
Later!

00:07:11.320 --> 00:07:14.660
I just can't believe you won't 
be going to the nationals.

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:16.930
Well, there's still the inter-high.

00:07:16.930 --> 00:07:18.830
I'm sure the break will do you good.

00:07:18.830 --> 00:07:23.580
What good does it do for<i> you </i>guys 
to worry about my standing?

00:07:23.580 --> 00:07:26.550
But it's important if you want to go pro, right?

00:07:26.550 --> 00:07:30.370
If you just do what you have to do, 
it'll all come together later.

00:07:30.370 --> 00:07:35.240
Personally, I care more about 
avenging my loss to Maruo.

00:07:35.670 --> 00:07:36.720
That's why I've decided

00:07:36.990 --> 00:07:39.220
to go abroad this year.

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:40.100
What?

00:07:40.440 --> 00:07:43.640
I'm thinking of leaving right after the inter-high.

00:07:43.640 --> 00:07:46.230
But... wh-where?

00:07:46.710 --> 00:07:49.490
Well, for tennis, it'll probably 
have to be America or Europe.

00:07:49.720 --> 00:07:51.110
Wait a second.

00:07:51.110 --> 00:07:53.220
This doesn't seem well thought-out.

00:07:53.220 --> 00:07:55.120
And what are you gonna do about school?

00:07:55.350 --> 00:07:57.320
Do you even have enough money?

00:07:57.320 --> 00:07:59.240
What about the language? And lifestyle?

00:07:59.770 --> 00:08:01.500
It'll all work out once I get there.

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:02.840
What?!

00:08:03.250 --> 00:08:06.500
It's not like I haven't given it any thought.

00:08:07.010 --> 00:08:12.260
I have to change my training and strategy 
according to what my circumstances are.

00:08:12.260 --> 00:08:14.470
I agree with that, but...

00:08:14.710 --> 00:08:18.320
Right now, my body is still maturing.

00:08:18.320 --> 00:08:22.920
I want to play against some top-level 
overseas players while I'm still growing.

00:08:22.920 --> 00:08:25.850
I was having trouble deciding when 
to go, but I just decided now!

00:08:26.420 --> 00:08:28.860
I'll come back an even bigger man.

00:08:31.240 --> 00:08:32.710
You'd better stay in touch.

00:08:32.710 --> 00:08:35.910
No matter where you go, 
we'll be cheering for you.

00:08:35.910 --> 00:08:37.190
Thanks!

00:08:39.460 --> 00:08:41.410
Bro!

00:08:41.900 --> 00:08:43.470
I won!

00:08:43.470 --> 00:08:46.290
I'm going to the All-Japan, too!

00:08:44.180 --> 00:08:46.290
First Nationals

00:08:46.290 --> 00:08:48.970
Really?! Congratulations, Yukichi-kun!

00:08:48.970 --> 00:08:50.710
It's all thanks to you, Bro!

00:08:50.710 --> 00:08:51.300
Huh?

00:08:51.590 --> 00:08:56.190
Well, no one pays attention to someone 
like me who doesn't want to go pro.

00:08:57.100 --> 00:09:01.310
I thought of how nervous you must've been, 
playing a match that would decide your future,

00:09:01.310 --> 00:09:02.940
and with all those eyes on you...

00:09:02.940 --> 00:09:07.190
But then I heard that instead of being 
nervous, you were out flirting!

00:09:07.190 --> 00:09:09.050
Everyone's talking about it, bigtime!

00:09:09.050 --> 00:09:10.070
What?

00:09:10.070 --> 00:09:11.980
See? I got this email.

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:17.430
After seeing this, I went beyond 
anger and sort of turned a corner.

00:09:17.430 --> 00:09:22.200
I don't know if that loosened me up 
or what, but I was on top of my game!

00:09:22.420 --> 00:09:26.210
6-4, 3-6, 6-4. I handled all the 
close battles and won swimmingly!

00:09:26.700 --> 00:09:29.630
I think I get how turning a corner like that feels.

00:09:29.630 --> 00:09:31.850
My dream finally came true!

00:09:32.860 --> 00:09:34.620
Congratulations.

00:09:34.620 --> 00:09:36.370
I'm so glad you won too, Bro!

00:09:36.370 --> 00:09:38.260
Let's do our best at the nationals!

00:09:38.500 --> 00:09:40.700
We need to get through the third round first.

00:09:41.170 --> 00:09:42.480
<i>That's right.</i>

00:09:42.480 --> 00:09:46.220
<i>By day two, the sixteen players going to the nationals are already decided.</i>

00:09:46.680 --> 00:09:51.020
<i>But now it's a battle for seed rankings 
at the All-Japan Junior.</i>

00:09:56.550 --> 00:10:01.030
All right, I'm gonna take them to the station, 
so you guys can use the baths first.

00:10:01.030 --> 00:10:02.470
Okay, we will.

00:10:02.470 --> 00:10:05.290
Nat-chan, everyone, good luck tomorrow!

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:07.290
Yeah. We'll do our best!

00:10:09.210 --> 00:10:10.950
<i>If you lose, you go home.</i>

00:10:10.950 --> 00:10:13.380
<i>I understand that, but it's still a harsh reality.</i>

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:16.650
<i>It means the nationals are just 
that high a hurdle to overcome.</i>

00:10:16.650 --> 00:10:18.300
<i>If I hadn't beaten Ide-kun,</i>

00:10:18.300 --> 00:10:20.180
<i>I wouldn't have overcome it myself.</i>

00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:27.980
It sure is a harsh world they live in.

00:10:27.980 --> 00:10:30.390
Ei-chan and the others 
are really working hard.

00:10:30.390 --> 00:10:31.080
Yeah.

00:10:32.020 --> 00:10:34.010
Should we be heading home, too?

00:10:34.010 --> 00:10:35.080
That sounds good.

00:10:35.710 --> 00:10:37.810
I'll give Ei-chan a call later.

00:10:37.810 --> 00:10:38.470
Okay.

00:10:42.070 --> 00:10:43.860
Okay, all done.

00:10:43.860 --> 00:10:44.880
Yukichi-kun!

00:10:45.580 --> 00:10:46.500
Huh?

00:10:47.240 --> 00:10:49.080
He's already fast asleep.

00:10:54.440 --> 00:10:55.800
Ei-chan, are you there?

00:10:59.560 --> 00:11:01.300
Nat-chan, what's up?

00:11:01.530 --> 00:11:06.060
It's nothing, really. I was just 
wondering what you were up to.

00:11:11.830 --> 00:11:13.270
Did you call home already?

00:11:13.270 --> 00:11:14.940
No, I'll do it later.

00:11:16.940 --> 00:11:21.370
Tell us how you feel now that 
you've successfully made it

00:11:21.370 --> 00:11:23.450
into the All-Japan Junior, Maruo.

00:11:23.450 --> 00:11:24.170
Huh?

00:11:24.610 --> 00:11:28.210
It's practice for your interview. Well?

00:11:32.300 --> 00:11:37.520
Today's match was very important for me 
in determining whether I can go pro,

00:11:37.520 --> 00:11:39.940
so I'm happy I won.

00:11:39.940 --> 00:11:42.710
Ide's play was not only difficult to predict,

00:11:42.710 --> 00:11:46.250
but very aggressive as well, 
so there were constant challenges.

00:11:46.250 --> 00:11:51.700
But what I learned from playing against 
Nat-chan a few months ago really helped.

00:11:51.700 --> 00:11:53.820
Anyway, I believe it was a great match

00:11:53.820 --> 00:11:57.690
in which I was able to give it my all 
against a truly powerful opponent.

00:11:57.690 --> 00:12:00.440
If I can, I would like to become stronger

00:12:00.670 --> 00:12:04.640
and play a match like that as a pro one day.

00:12:05.700 --> 00:12:07.590
Something like that?

00:12:11.460 --> 00:12:13.870
Wh-Why are you laughing?!

00:12:13.870 --> 00:12:16.950
Sorry! It was just so perfect.

00:12:16.950 --> 00:12:18.730
It wasn't too stiff?

00:12:18.730 --> 00:12:20.630
No, it was very you, Ei-chan!

00:12:20.630 --> 00:12:25.220
Oh, I'm changing the subject, 
but have you ever been in the zone?

00:12:25.510 --> 00:12:28.900
Oh, like being in the ideal 
state of mind while playing?

00:12:28.900 --> 00:12:31.880
I don't really know much about all that.

00:12:32.560 --> 00:12:36.520
There are some times when 
I play unbelievably well,

00:12:36.520 --> 00:12:41.830
but I don't know if that's because I'm 
in the zone or because of my training.

00:12:43.490 --> 00:12:46.990
<i>So it's something even a player at 
Nat-chan's level doesn't understand.</i>

00:12:47.430 --> 00:12:49.730
I wonder if it's when I can't even

00:12:49.730 --> 00:12:53.580
hear a big crowd because 
I'm concentrating so hard.

00:12:53.580 --> 00:12:55.270
That's how it feels?

00:12:55.830 --> 00:13:01.200
<i>Come to think of it, Nat-chan's matches 
draw crowds like Ide-kun's, too.</i>

00:13:01.200 --> 00:13:04.280
<i>I bet she's experienced a lot of those matches.</i>

00:13:04.700 --> 00:13:05.840
<i>She's strong...</i>

00:13:06.260 --> 00:13:07.640
<i>And she's cute.</i>

00:13:08.260 --> 00:13:11.130
<i>I'm dating </i>that<i> Nat-chan...</i>

00:13:13.100 --> 00:13:15.910
I... I wonder if it'll be hot tomorrow, too.

00:13:15.910 --> 00:13:18.150
It's supposed to be about the same as today.

00:13:18.150 --> 00:13:20.570
Oh... I see.

00:13:20.570 --> 00:13:21.900
I didn't see the forecast.

00:13:21.900 --> 00:13:25.150
That's no good. People who 
won today should check.

00:13:25.150 --> 00:13:26.580
Y-Yeah...

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:31.650
<i>What does it mean to date someone?</i>

00:13:32.160 --> 00:13:34.410
<i>It feels like nothing's really changed,</i>

00:13:34.670 --> 00:13:36.970
<i>but it also feels like something 
between us is different.</i>

00:13:38.840 --> 00:13:43.800
<i>I wonder if holding my hand like 
that just happens naturally. or...</i>

00:13:47.700 --> 00:13:56.180
Reason

00:13:48.100 --> 00:13:51.410
<i>No, no, this obviously isn't the right time.</i>

00:13:51.890 --> 00:13:56.180
<i>But Nat-chan's hands were so soft...</i>

00:13:52.700 --> 00:13:56.180
Instinct

00:13:59.010 --> 00:14:01.020
<i>No! I have to keep my head!</i>

00:14:05.650 --> 00:14:09.110
<i>I sometimes feel like my instincts 
are outweighing my reason lately.</i>

00:14:14.760 --> 00:14:15.200
Here.

00:14:15.200 --> 00:14:18.210
<i>Huh?! Does she know what 
I was thinking about?</i>

00:14:18.210 --> 00:14:21.800
Here, hurry! Put your hand on top.

00:14:21.800 --> 00:14:22.460
On top?

00:14:23.710 --> 00:14:26.360
All right, we're gonna do 
our best again tomorrow!

00:14:26.360 --> 00:14:28.250
Here we go!

00:14:28.250 --> 00:14:29.720
Go!

00:14:30.220 --> 00:14:34.080
<i>Is this... okay? Or what?</i>

00:14:41.460 --> 00:14:46.700
Okay, it's now a battle between the strongest 
players who made it into the All-Japan Junior.

00:14:46.700 --> 00:14:49.990
You're all aware that this next match 
will determine what seed you'll get?

00:14:49.990 --> 00:14:50.740
Yes!

00:14:51.470 --> 00:14:55.510
Today's results will heavily influence 
your position in the All-Japan Junior.

00:14:55.510 --> 00:14:59.000
Consider today the beginning 
of the All-Japan Junior.

00:14:59.000 --> 00:15:00.000
Yes!

00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:04.500
Yukichi-kun, you sure are fired up.

00:15:05.190 --> 00:15:07.460
This time, I'll go as far as I can!

00:15:07.460 --> 00:15:10.510
Let's both win today and 
meet up in the fourth round!

00:15:10.830 --> 00:15:12.410
Yeah, let's do it.

00:15:12.410 --> 00:15:16.410
That being said, my opponent's pretty tough.

00:15:17.480 --> 00:15:19.020
Good morning, Maruo-kun.

00:15:19.020 --> 00:15:20.920
Nabae-kun, good morning.

00:15:20.920 --> 00:15:23.270
That was a great match against Ide yesterday.

00:15:23.610 --> 00:15:24.850
Thanks.

00:15:24.850 --> 00:15:28.030
I was able to calm down after 
I noticed you were there.

00:15:28.570 --> 00:15:29.650
Oh, right...

00:15:29.650 --> 00:15:31.030
Hey, Takagi!

00:15:31.030 --> 00:15:31.810
Huh?

00:15:33.720 --> 00:15:35.180
What do you want, Nabae?

00:15:35.180 --> 00:15:38.330
This is Takagi Sakuya. He's from my club.

00:15:38.330 --> 00:15:40.290
He's up against Fukazawa-kun today.

00:15:40.870 --> 00:15:45.540
I thought I should introduce you, since you 
might end up playing him in the fourth round.

00:15:45.540 --> 00:15:47.460
Oh, is that so?

00:15:48.090 --> 00:15:51.180
<i>This is the fourth seed, Takagi Sakuya.</i>

00:15:51.180 --> 00:15:53.940
Maruo, as in... Oh.

00:15:55.450 --> 00:15:56.310
So?

00:15:56.310 --> 00:15:56.850
Huh?

00:15:57.380 --> 00:15:58.840
Is that it?

00:15:58.840 --> 00:16:00.060
Yeah, that's it.

00:16:00.060 --> 00:16:02.170
I know who he is.

00:16:02.170 --> 00:16:03.950
Then introduce yourself.

00:16:04.950 --> 00:16:08.070
You're as meticulous as ever.

00:16:09.110 --> 00:16:12.620
Sorry about that. He's a really good player, but...

00:16:13.110 --> 00:16:14.020
Well, see you.

00:16:14.020 --> 00:16:14.820
Yeah.

00:16:15.060 --> 00:16:17.280
Hey, Takagi, wait a second.

00:16:17.280 --> 00:16:18.580
Huh?

00:16:18.580 --> 00:16:20.880
They <i>are</i> close, right?

00:16:20.880 --> 00:16:25.020
Bro, I really don't like that Takagi guy.

00:16:25.020 --> 00:16:25.830
Huh?

00:16:26.180 --> 00:16:30.330
He was really rude for someone 
meeting you for the first time.

00:16:31.370 --> 00:16:33.720
Just because he beat Nabae once...

00:16:33.720 --> 00:16:37.150
What? That guy beat Nabae-kun?

00:16:37.150 --> 00:16:39.720
Oh? You didn't know?

00:16:40.520 --> 00:16:45.350
Takagi beat Nabae once, in an 
unofficial tournament at their club.

00:16:45.350 --> 00:16:46.530
What?

00:16:46.530 --> 00:16:50.380
<i>I can't believe it. Nabae-kun lost...</i>

00:16:51.930 --> 00:16:56.240
But I'll defeat Takagi, so you 
have to win today too, Bro!

00:16:57.050 --> 00:16:58.410
Then we'll have our first

00:16:58.410 --> 00:17:00.950
official match against each 
other in the fourth round!

00:17:00.950 --> 00:17:01.720
Yeah!

00:17:02.630 --> 00:17:04.480
<i>First I have to get through the third round!</i>

00:17:05.210 --> 00:17:10.000
<i>Ono Kazuma. He's the eleventh seed and 
made the top four in the Chiba prefectural.</i>

00:17:10.210 --> 00:17:12.460
<i>Even though he favors 
hitting risky flat shots,</i>

00:17:12.460 --> 00:17:15.260
<i>he makes very few mistakes and 
corners you with ground strokes.</i>

00:17:15.640 --> 00:17:18.470
<i>He's also a skilled defensive player, 
so I can't attack carelessly.</i>

00:17:19.010 --> 00:17:21.580
<i>What's important when facing 
opponents like this is</i>

00:17:21.580 --> 00:17:24.230
<i>how well I can maintain my attack style.</i>

00:17:25.570 --> 00:17:27.480
Best of three set match.

00:17:28.050 --> 00:17:29.480
Maruo to serve.

00:17:29.480 --> 00:17:31.580
<i>As expected from a seeded player.</i>

00:17:31.580 --> 00:17:33.230
<i>There are a lot of people here to watch.</i>

00:17:33.850 --> 00:17:38.050
<i>But compared to my match against 
Ide-kun, there's less pressure.</i>

00:17:38.050 --> 00:17:40.960
<i>First, I have to hit my serve
in just the right spot,</i>

00:17:41.510 --> 00:17:44.370
<i>learn how he plays at my own pace,</i>

00:17:44.370 --> 00:17:46.870
<i>and hold serve in this first game!</i>

00:17:49.040 --> 00:17:49.970
<i>It's in!</i>

00:17:51.810 --> 00:17:53.040
<i>A strong flat shot.</i>

00:17:53.040 --> 00:17:55.050
<i>But I won't miss a shallow hit!</i>

00:17:56.570 --> 00:17:58.220
<i>If that doesn't do it, then...</i>

00:18:01.000 --> 00:18:02.220
15-love.

00:18:02.220 --> 00:18:03.220
Yes!

00:18:04.270 --> 00:18:07.370
<i>Even if his reaction is slow, 
he makes up for it with his fast legs</i>

00:18:07.370 --> 00:18:09.930
<i>and hits back harder than I expect.</i>

00:18:10.470 --> 00:18:12.230
That's the way, Maruo!

00:18:12.680 --> 00:18:15.980
Even though he's not seeded, I heard 
he's number two in Kanagawa.

00:18:15.980 --> 00:18:18.490
That match against Ide yesterday was amazing.

00:18:19.120 --> 00:18:22.080
<i>Th-There are people here to watch me?!</i>

00:18:22.080 --> 00:18:24.490
<i>No, no! Don't get distracted by that!</i>

00:18:27.950 --> 00:18:29.890
<i>I just need to play like I always do.</i>

00:18:30.250 --> 00:18:31.290
<i>Here I go!</i>

00:18:38.870 --> 00:18:41.600
Game, set, and match. Winner: Maruo.

00:18:41.600 --> 00:18:44.010
Score: 6-3, 6-3.

00:18:42.580 --> 00:18:43.510
Yes!

00:18:44.010 --> 00:18:45.770
All right, good job!

00:18:46.100 --> 00:18:50.260
But then again, you beat Ide-kun, 
so there was no way you'd lose today.

00:18:50.260 --> 00:18:51.000
Right.

00:18:51.620 --> 00:18:53.020
Depressed

00:18:53.020 --> 00:18:55.570
I-I'm so crushed.

00:18:56.260 --> 00:18:59.920
I wanted to... I wanted to play 
a match against you, Bro.

00:18:59.920 --> 00:19:01.170
Yukichi-kun...

00:19:02.410 --> 00:19:08.160
Bro! That Takagi guy is really, 
<i>really </i>nasty, so be careful!

00:19:08.160 --> 00:19:10.980
Yukichi-kun, you keep saying that.

00:19:11.560 --> 00:19:13.840
What exactly do you mean?

00:19:13.840 --> 00:19:17.420
That punk was leading 4-2 in the first set,

00:19:17.420 --> 00:19:20.700
and he hit an unnecessary and 
unexpected underhand serve!

00:19:21.680 --> 00:19:23.090
{A: scoreboard}Takagi Sakuya
Fukazawa Yukichi

00:19:29.560 --> 00:19:30.430
40-love.

00:19:33.810 --> 00:19:35.610
That pisses me off!

00:19:35.630 --> 00:19:36.890
I got it on video.

00:19:36.890 --> 00:19:38.640
Oh, thanks.

00:19:39.190 --> 00:19:42.090
But I've done that before, too.

00:19:42.090 --> 00:19:44.780
I think it's something you 
have to do if you want to win.

00:19:44.780 --> 00:19:47.370
What you did is different from this!

00:19:47.370 --> 00:19:51.870
Normally, you do something like that to 
throw off an opponent who's much stronger,

00:19:51.870 --> 00:19:55.840
or to calmly but forcibly change the pace!

00:19:56.050 --> 00:19:58.840
There's no reason to do 
that when you're winning!

00:19:58.840 --> 00:20:01.590
But why would he do such a thing?

00:20:01.860 --> 00:20:04.930
It's obviously because he was 
trying to make me look bad!

00:20:04.930 --> 00:20:06.640
He broke my serve and had a two-game lead,

00:20:06.640 --> 00:20:09.220
so he wanted to toy with me!

00:20:10.280 --> 00:20:12.230
<i>Is that really true?</i>

00:20:12.790 --> 00:20:17.240
That being said, he's the fourth seed, 
so he was a strong opponent anyway.

00:20:16.540 --> 00:20:20.190
Takagi Sakuya

00:20:17.240 --> 00:20:20.190
In the end, I lost because 
of my lack of ability.

00:20:20.460 --> 00:20:23.830
That's why you <i>have</i> to avenge me, okay, Bro?!

00:20:23.830 --> 00:20:26.570
Y-Yeah. I'll try my best.

00:20:27.350 --> 00:20:29.330
Takagi Sakuya, eh?

00:20:29.810 --> 00:20:32.440
From what I see in his match with Yukichi,

00:20:32.440 --> 00:20:36.580
he seems like an all-rounder who's devoted 
to fundamentals and has few blind spots.

00:20:36.580 --> 00:20:39.040
<i>It's true. I can tell he's strong.</i>

00:20:39.040 --> 00:20:42.600
<i>But how did this guy beat Nabae-kun?</i>

00:20:45.850 --> 00:20:47.400
Oh, Takagi.

00:20:47.400 --> 00:20:49.350
Congrats on making it to the fourth round.

00:20:49.840 --> 00:20:53.860
You usually overshadow me, 
but I'm the fourth seed, after all.

00:21:00.740 --> 00:21:01.730
Good morning!

00:21:01.730 --> 00:21:04.240
Hey, right on time as usual!

00:21:04.500 --> 00:21:05.780
Good morning!

00:21:05.780 --> 00:21:06.990
Morning!

00:21:12.420 --> 00:21:13.870
What are you writing?

00:21:13.870 --> 00:21:18.240
I'm identifying what my current situation 
is like, and things I want to improve.

00:21:18.240 --> 00:21:20.750
I'll use it as a reference for my next practice.

00:21:21.140 --> 00:21:26.210
<i>Nabae's thorough self-analysis and pursuit 
of the fundamentals were impeccable.</i>

00:21:30.090 --> 00:21:33.910
<i>Repeating that process made 
Nabae stronger and stronger.</i>

00:21:34.610 --> 00:21:38.390
<i>I also climbed up to this 
level by following Nabae.</i>

00:21:39.150 --> 00:21:41.150
What's wrong, Takagi?

00:21:41.450 --> 00:21:45.400
I'm gonna make it to the top so 
I can beat you one more time.

00:21:46.890 --> 00:21:48.390
Better do your best.

00:21:48.390 --> 00:21:51.030
There's no excuse for the 
first seed messing up.

00:21:51.030 --> 00:21:53.040
Yeah. I will.

00:21:54.520 --> 00:21:56.850
<i>To win the All-Japan Junior,</i>

00:21:56.850 --> 00:21:59.540
<i>I want to play against Nabae-kun 
in Kanto, no matter what.</i>

00:21:59.930 --> 00:22:03.350
<i>And to do that, I have to beat this guy first.</i>

00:22:04.550 --> 00:22:06.800
Kanto Junior Tennis Arena

00:22:04.550 --> 00:22:06.800
4th Round

00:22:12.550 --> 00:22:15.460
<i>That's a rather casual way 
of deciding who serves.</i>

00:22:15.460 --> 00:22:16.560
Okay, bottom.

00:22:16.560 --> 00:22:17.830
Top it is.

00:22:18.380 --> 00:22:19.560
My serve.

00:22:20.170 --> 00:22:22.400
<i>He didn't even check. He already knew.</i>

00:22:23.050 --> 00:22:24.850
<i>Regardless, I have to win.</i>

00:22:25.380 --> 00:22:26.320
Good luck.

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:25.020
Next Time

00:24:00.420 --> 00:24:03.370
What really bothers me is that

00:24:03.370 --> 00:24:05.900
he's been glaring at me this whole time!

00:24:05.900 --> 00:24:08.840
Wait, this isn't the time to
think about how strange he is!

00:24:08.840 --> 00:24:10.830
I need to be more composed 
at times like these.

00:24:10.830 --> 00:24:13.610
I shouldn't let him get to me every time.

00:24:13.610 --> 00:24:15.680
He seems like he'll fall for it, but he doesn't.

00:24:15.680 --> 00:24:17.770
But I won't lose this match.

00:24:17.770 --> 00:24:20.680
I'm going to face Nabae, no matter what!

00:24:20.680 --> 00:24:22.580
Next time on <i>Baby Steps</i>,

00:24:21.540 --> 00:24:25.020
Psychological Warfare and Self-Control

00:24:22.580 --> 00:24:24.370
"Psychological Warfare and Self-Control."

00:24:25.210 --> 00:24:31.000
End
